          %hr/
          %h2#20090831 2009-08-31
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    made
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimal space
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+quantity"} infinitesimal quantity
                    redirect to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal object
                    – this way we can use the links and still wait with deciding whether to split the latter entry or not
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+algebra"} cosimplicial algebra
                    (redirecting also
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+ring"} cosimplicial ring
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra+in+synthetic+differential+geometry"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra in synthetic differential geometry
                    where I aim to derive the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                    of a Lie group
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                    in terms of functions on the infinitesimal neighbourhood of the identity in a manner entirely analogous to how the deRham dgca is obtained at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+in+synthetic+differential+geometry"} differential forms in synthetic differential geometry
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+singular+simplicial+complex"} infinitesimal singular simplicial complex
                    – it reiterates things said at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+in+synthetic+differential+geometry"} differential forms in synthetic differential geometry
                    but the motivation for creating it was to accomodate a reference that
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+Skoda"} Zoran Skoda
                    provided which gives a version of this notion in
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} nonstandard analysis
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jon+Awbrey"} Jon Awbrey
                added a stub and a link for future development at
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peirce%27s+logic+of+information"} Peirce's logic of information
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    created an
                    %em Idea
                    section at
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+and+quantity"} space and quantity
                  %p Given the pivotal role that this entry is playing I am unhappy with its rough appearance. Hope we can eventually improve on that.
                %li
                  %p
                    replied to Toby at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal object
                    by agreeing that, yes, now that you mention it, it sounds like a good idea to rename that entry into
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimal space
                    and create a parallel entry
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+quantity"} infinitesimal quantity
                %li
                  %p thanks to Toby for the rephrasing, it’s much better now, yes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"}> Toby Bartels
                \:
              %ul
                %li Rephrased (and tightened) the second warning above to what I think is the important point.
                %li
                  Cross linked
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+theory"} relation theory
                %li
                  An introductory question at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal object
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \: various very minor edits:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    added a first sentence at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+bundle"} twisted bundle
                    that links the concept with
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
                    (but more details could be given on that)
                %li
                  %p
                    slightly edited the beginning of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree dga
                    (added the statement for the graded-commutative case)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \: there was some funny behaviour by the software ater I had restarted the server a few minutes ago, which resulted in the Lab-Elf announcement below to disappear for some mysterious reason. I have rolled back now, but that, too, involved some funny effects. It should all be restored now, but if anyone wonders where his or her comment disappeared to, it may have been eaten by the software in this process (but I don’t think anything is lost, but let me know).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    added to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+in+synthetic+differential+geometry"} differential forms in synthetic differential geometry
                    references by Breen-Messing and by Kock with a few lines of remarks. Am hoping to eventually expand and polish this entry.
                %li
                  %p
                    slightly edited the first paragraphs of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal object
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} nonstandard analysis
                    and inserted links back and forth
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Lab Elf (public relations)
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Lab+Elf"} ?
                \: the migration will happen this week. I had hoped to get everything done before the semester started at the Cobblers School, but was not able to do so, which means it has to fit in around my schedule. What I don’t want to do is do the migration, then go off for another violin lesson, and come back a few hours later to find that you’ve all crashed the site again.
              %p
                Once that has been done, then the technical department can get on with figuring out how to improve things around here. However, whinging on this page is pretty pointless. If there’s some feature you’d like implemented then you could bug the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"} Chief Lab Elf
                himself (though rumour has it that he’s quite busy at the moment) or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Stacey"} one of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"} the minions
                %strong much better idea
                would be to start a discussion about it over on the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ntnu.no/~stacey/Mathforge/nForum/"} n-Forum
                = succeed "." do
                  %em lab elf notice board
                %strong all
                denizens of the lab to see, put it here, but if it’s primarily for the lab elves, put it on the forum.
              %p (Note: the high honour of being a Lab Elf is one that anyone can have. There are various sub-departments, all with different roles and skills.)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \: replied to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rafael+Borowiecki"} Rafael Borowiecki
                at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
              %p following various suggestions I didn’t quite delete the big discussion box there yet, but instead moved it to the very end of the entry, so that it doesn’t interrupt the reading flow anymore where it used to be (since we reached agreement there).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \: replied to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rafael+Borowiecki"} Rafael Borowiecki
                at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
                and asked for further details
              %ul
                %li
                  %p I second John’s and Toby’s comments: the reason why it is important to log changes here is because this is the only reasonable way that we alert each other of changes and thereby give us a chance to interact with each other. If nobody would log here, everybody would be bound to blindly edit the Lab on his or her own, whithout any interaction. I have added a remark to this extent now also to the blurb that appears on the top of this page.
                  %p And yes, we are all suffering from the slowness of the Lab. But the moment that Andrew Stacey decides he is ready, we will switch to a better server. He has already set up everything and is just waiting for a good moment to migrate.
            %li
              %p
