                        among other things this aims to provide the full general nonsense
                        = succeed "-version" do
                          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                            %semantics
                              %mrow
                                %mn ∞
                              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
                    %li
                      %p I could move this to my private web. Let me know if you feel that would be better.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"}> Zoran Škoda
                \: created
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+profunctor"} crossed profunctor
                (of crossed modules) and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/butterfly"} butterfly
                (papillon). First after M. Jibladze (1990) and second after B. Noohi (2005). I did not draw the diagram but wrote equations explicitly.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric"}> Eric
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Gleefully responded to John’s gleeful response on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"}> Zoran Škoda
                \: created
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reconstruction+theorem"} reconstruction theorem
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                  \: I love the idea of an article full of
                  = succeed "!" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reconstruction+theorems"} reconstruction theorems
                  = succeed "-linear" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi FinVect
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinVect_k
                  is equivalent to the category of finite-dimensional representations of some coalgebra. Does anyone know a reference to this sort of theorem? It’s crucial that we use
                  = succeed "algebras" do
                    %em co
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    added something on the dual Dold-Kan correspondence relating
                    %em co
                    \-chain complexes and co-simplicial abelian groups to
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
                %li
                  %p
                    renamed differentials at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
                    from “
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
                    ” to “
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial
                    ”
                %li
                  %p
                    expanded
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+in+synthetic+differential+geometry"} differential forms in synthetic differential geometry
                    with two purposes: it reviews the definition found in the literature and then proposes a – supposedly nicer – reformulation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"}> Zoran Škoda
                \: added a query in
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
                = succeed "-modules" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    Added theorem characterizing categories of
                    = succeed "-modules" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi R
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
                %li
                  %p
                    Added same theorem and also the Mitchell embedding theorem to
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
                %li
                  %p
                    Gleefully shot down an idea of Eric’s over at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
                    — but this idea can be resuscitated using the concept of ‘resolution’.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sridhar+Ramesh"} Sridhar Ramesh
                added a small note that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topologies
                are the same as (internal) closure operators on truth values (Being new here, I’m not exactly sure what the protocols are; in “Please log all your non-trivial changes”, does “non-trivial” mean everything above, say, typo-correction?). I also observed, in the article on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C, Set]^{op} \to Set
                is representable just in case it is limit-preserving).
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                    \: I added a remark to the text above on what “non-trivial” means. Generally, I think you can’t log too much of your activity here, just too little. So if in doubt whether anyone else might be interested in your changes or not, drop a note here.
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                    \: Welcome, Sridhar Ramesh! I’d like to add: we are not trying to force you to do lots of bureaucratic work, so please don’t feel we are
                    %em demanding
                    you to log changes here. If you make a change and feel too tired to log it here, we won’t be mad at you. We just
                    %em like
                    to see changes here, even smallish ones.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric"}> Eric
                \: Asked a question of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike
                (or anyone else interested in SDG) at
                = succeed "." do
